<title>BELGIUM: EU grain panel spotlight on Spanish maize imports.</title>
<headline>EU grain panel spotlight on Spanish maize imports.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preferential maize imports into Spain will be the main tender item at the weekly meeting of the European Union cereals management committee on Thursday, EU officials said.</p>
<p>The EU has ended other 1996/97 (July/June) grain tenders. It could open tenders for next season at the end of June but is not expected to be in any hurry to grant export licences.</p>
<p>Last week the EU rejected all bids to import maize into Spain at a reduced tariff.</p>
<p>It also reduced the quota, which compensates U.S. exporters for trade losses after Spain joined the EU in 1986, to 550,000 tonnes, from 800,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>The reduction followed an upwards revision in estimated Spanish imports of grain substitutes, such as corn gluten feed. --Brussels newsroom +322 287 6830</p>
</text>
